After the grocery store, I stop at a nearby vegetable cart.
There are many fresh vegetables on the cart.
There are still a few things left on my list.
I say to the vegetable vendor, "Bhaiya, please give me a quarter kilo of onions."
He puts the onions in a basket.
Then I ask him for green chilies.
"Bhaiya, please also give fifty grams of fresh green chilies."
He weighs the green chilies.
After that, I need a lemon.
I see a big yellow lemon on the cart.
I say, "Please put in this one lemon too."
Finally, I need green coriander.
I say, "Bhaiya, please give some fresh green coriander too."
Bhaiya keeps the coriander in my basket too.
I check the list in my mind.
First onions, then green chilies, after that lemon and coriander.
Yes, my list is complete.
I ask, "Bhaiya, how much money in total?"
He says, "Madam, sixty rupees in total."
I give him the money and walk towards home.
